# CPS-Visualizer Release Notes
## 1.2.3 (8 Aug 2026)

### Improvements
* Distance panel layout: 2x4 grid (6 heatmaps + dedicated colorbar cell)
  with even spacing — heatmaps no longer pushed to the right side
* Wider canvas (12x6) to accommodate the 2x4 layout

## 1.2.2 (8 Aug 2026)

### Fixes
* **Crash-proof exception handling** — all unhandled exceptions (including
  Qt slot errors and macOS IMK input-method errors) now show a message box
  instead of killing the application
* Global ``sys.excepthook`` + ``CPSApplication.notify`` override catches
  errors in signal/slot callbacks and the main thread
* Startup failures show a clear error dialog rather than a silent abort

## 1.2.1 (8 Aug 2026)

### Major Features
* **`cpsv` unified command** — `pip install -e ./` in the `cpsvisualizer/` directory registers a system `cpsv` entry point:
  `cpsv` (default = batch CLI), `cpsv gui`, `cpsv web --port 6789`
* New packaging via modern setuptools `pyproject.toml` (editable install supported)
* **Grayscale-ink visualization** for element maps: minimum values are colourless (transparent) and only the deepest values render as dark grayscale; robust `display_scale` (log1p + percentile window) prevents outliers from flattening the maps
* **Distance panel** now shows a 2x3 grid of six representative normalized (0-1) distance heatmaps at once
* **Comparison pane** redesigned as a 2x2 grid of square PCA / t-SNE / UMAP / K-Means scatter plots with a full-width dendrogram on top
* Cross-shape datasets (Geology, Bivalve shell, Tissue) can now be compared together — each matrix is flattened and resampled to a common length for PCA / t-SNE / UMAP and distance metrics
* Element-map and distance screenshots are generated per DataSample sub-directory (Geology / Bivalve / Tissue)

### Fixes
* Render Mode combo now actually updates the active render mode (enhanced / filtered were silently ignored before)
* Empty-data guards in the distance heatmap / `display_scale` prevent crashes on clear/reload
* Cleaner element naming in the GUI (full file stem is kept, so `Tissue_Fe57` no longer collides with `Tissue_P31`)


## 1.3.0 (7 Aug 2026)

### Major Features
* **Cross-disciplinary sample suite** — public LA-ICP-MS element/Ca growth-line profiles of bivalve shells (cockle & clam) from Zenodo (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18873283), demonstrating applicability beyond geology
* Web "Load Sample" menu now offers both geological and marine-biology sample suites
* Sample endpoint `POST /api/sample/<id>` loads bundled data directories server-side
* Distance endpoint downsamples + aligns datasets to a common shape so cross-shaped samples compare cleanly

## 1.2.0 (7 Aug 2026)

### Major Features
* New `web.py` — Flask web interface with drag-and-drop upload, dark/light themes, Plotly visualisations
* **Map Viewer** — full-scan element maps at true data aspect ratio (strict square cells), dataset cycling, Raw / Enhanced / Filtered render modes, and a **wipe compare** that drags a divider across any two maps
* 6 new spatial filters / normalisers shared by all interfaces: gaussian_filter, median_filter, sobel_gradient, unsharp_mask, normalize_01, clip_percentile
* **AODA continuous optimisation** — Box-Cox power exponent tuned by combining golden-section search and secant (quasi-Newton) method; the higher-DPS winner is reported; cheap metric pre-screening keeps it fast
* Endpoint result caching (versioned, LRU-capped) — repeated tab visits return instantly

### Improvements
* Square-cell rendering everywhere: GUI / CLI / `visualization.py` now use `aspect='equal'`
* GUI adds **Wipe Compare** toolbar action (two datasets + draggable slider)
* **GUI Map Viewer** — mirrors the Web interface: step datasets with ‹/›, render raw / enhanced / filtered, wipe-compare any two maps with a draggable divider; follows the native system theme
* GUI gains Analysis tabs (Statistics / Comparison / Image Quality / AODA) with PCA, correlation, t-SNE, UMAP, dendrogram, K-means, quality bars and AODA continuous optimisation
* Web map plots set explicit `width`/`height` from the true data aspect ratio so square data renders square
* Vectorized `_downsample` (block-mean via reshape) replaces the Python double loop
* Web distance/all, comparison, metrics, adaptive and benchmark endpoints are cached

## 1.1.0 (7 Aug 2026)

### Major Features
* New `core.py` module — shared distance metrics, transforms, and utilities eliminating all code duplication between GUI and CLI (26 distance functions, 6 transforms)
* New `statistics.py` module — PCA, Pearson/Spearman correlation, ANOVA, Kruskal-Wallis, descriptive statistics, uncertainty quantification
* New `metrics.py` module — PSNR, Shannon entropy, Contrast Enhancement Index, Tenengrad sharpness, multi-scale SSIM evaluation
* New `comparison.py` module — PCA, t-SNE, UMAP, hierarchical clustering, K-means comparison against established methods
* New `visualization.py` module — publication-quality figure generation (PCA scatter, t-SNE/UMAP embeddings, dendrograms, correlation heatmaps, image quality charts)
* Two new continuous distance metrics: Bray-Curtis and Canberra

### Improvements
* Complete architectural refactor — dict-based dispatch replaces 26+ thin wrapper methods in both GUI and CLI
* Fixed critical bug: dataset `j` incorrectly reshaped to dataset `i`'s shape in pairwise loops
* Fixed division-by-zero guards in Cosine, Correlation, and z-score normalization
* Fixed Minkowski default parameter from p=3 to standard p=2
* Fixed subplot layout — now uses optimal rectangular grid instead of wasteful perfect squares
* GUI: removed unused Qt5 import from CLI, cleaned all unused imports, added docstrings and type hints
* CLI: improved argument handling, silent skip of unrecognized transform names
* `visual_diff` now returns Figure object instead of leaking via pyplot state machine
* Removed ~150 lines of dead code (stale mutual_info function, bare list expressions, unused wrapper)

### Testing
* 100 comprehensive unit tests covering all modules: transforms, 28 distance metrics, pairwise computation, statistics, image quality metrics, comparison methods, visualization output, CLI workflow, and edge cases (zero data, constant data, shape mismatches, NaN propagation)

## 0.0.1 (10 Jul 2024)

* Initial release
